==============================================================================
P1  LINK 2 (polymer): the ONLY large-field slack, union bound -> Kotecky-Preiss
==============================================================================
  N=2: c*_union=29.85 (t*=5.46)   c**_KP=22.39 (t**=4.73)
        improvement factor c*/c** = 1.3333  (= d lnL/ln(2d) at L=2)
        in t*: 1.1547   in admissible g^2: 1.3333
  N=3: c*_union=19.90 (t*=4.46)   c**_KP=14.93 (t**=3.86)
        improvement factor c*/c** = 1.3333  (= d lnL/ln(2d) at L=2)
        in t*: 1.1547   in admissible g^2: 1.3333
        NOTE: c**_KP = ln(2d)/(2 beta0) is L-INDEPENDENT; c*_union = d lnL/(2 beta0)
              grows with L  =>  L=2 is the optimal integer blocking factor:
              L=2: c*_union= 19.90   c*/c**_KP = 1.333
              L=3: c*_union= 31.54   c*/c**_KP = 2.113
              L=4: c*_union= 39.80   c*/c**_KP = 2.667

==============================================================================
P2  UNIT CONVERSION: the corpus has THREE objects called 'lambda'
==============================================================================
   (R1) lambda = g^2            [CPB-preprint §3.3: 'with the coupling as expansion parameter']
   (R2) lambda = lambda_tH=betaN [ch13-machine.tex: crossover at lambda_tH in [1,7.3]]
   (R3) lambda = beta            [lattice]

                          point |    beta |      g^2 |  lambda_tH
   --- N=2 ---
          SZZ radius  beta=1/48 |  0.0208 |  192.000 |      0.042
    crossover LOW edge lam_tH=1 |  0.5000 |    8.000 |      1.000
        physical point beta=2.4 |  2.4000 |    1.667 |      4.800
        physical point beta=2.5 |  2.5000 |    1.600 |      5.000
         lambda_tH = 7.3 (ch13) |  3.6500 |    1.096 |      7.300
    g^2 = 1  (Balaban marginal) |  4.0000 |    1.000 |      8.000
   --- N=3 ---
          SZZ radius  beta=1/48 |  0.0208 |  288.000 |      0.062
    crossover LOW edge lam_tH=1 |  0.3333 |   18.000 |      1.000
        physical point beta=2.4 |  2.4000 |    2.500 |      7.200
        physical point beta=2.5 |  2.5000 |    2.400 |      7.500
         lambda_tH = 7.3 (ch13) |  2.4333 |    2.466 |      7.300
    g^2 = 1  (Balaban marginal) |  6.0000 |    1.000 |     18.000

   => 'lambda ~ 1' (R1, g^2 ~ 1) is lambda_tH = 2N^2 = 8 (N=2), 18 (N=3).
   => 'lambda_tH = 1' is g^2 = 2N^2 = 8 (N=2), 18 (N=3).
      The two '1's differ by exactly 2N^2.  They are NOT the same number.

